From 2650afeb7de89ed3f8114d2b2b597287c5f273fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild Idler Patch <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:24:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Confirm asset licensing covers a sold, compiled game --
 resolved

Actual license text for all four in-use asset packs (item icons, hero
sprites, fox pet, dog pet) was provided directly and checked against
the specific question: does this cover shipping a compiled, commercially
sold game (Steam or otherwise)? All four are unambiguously fine --
none restrict how a finished game is distributed, only whether the raw
asset files can be resold/repackaged as a standalone pack, which every
license text explicitly separates from 'part of a project'/'a game
using this.' No asset currently in use needs replacing or re-licensing
before a Steam launch.

Also notes a small future Credits/About screen idea in Brainstorming,
since 3 of the 4 packs specifically appreciate (though don't require)
credit.

Documentation-only change -- no code touched.
